.TH USB-PROTECTION 1 "September 2026" "USB Protection 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-protection \- manage USB device access from the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-protection
.SH DESCRIPTION
USB Protection is a GTK4 and Libadwaita interface for USBGuard.
It lists connected devices and provides temporary and persistent allow
operations, blocking, and saved rule management.
Run it in an ordinary graphical user session, never as root.
Administrative operations use the system authentication agent.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/usbguard/rules.conf
.RS
Existing USBGuard policy, preserved by installation and removal.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usbguard (1),
.BR usb-protection-agent (1)
